  <h2>Sustainable Performance</h2>
  <p>Modern consumers are increasingly conscious of their environmental footprint. Eco-friendly activewear is no longer a niche—it's a requirement for many premium brands.</p>
  
  <h3>Recycled Materials (RPET & Econyl)</h3>
  <p>Recycled Polyester (RPET) is made from plastic bottles, while Econyl is regenerated nylon from ocean waste like fishing nets. Both offer the same performance as virgin fibers but with a fraction of the environmental impact.</p>

  <h3>Natural Alternatives</h3>
  <p>Bamboo and Organic Cotton are becoming popular for "Active-Life" wear. They offer natural breathability and are biodegradable.</p>

  <h3>Marketing Your Mission</h3>
  <p>Don't just use green fabrics—tell the story. Use GRS (Global Recycled Standard) certifications to back up your claims and build authentic trust with your audience.</p>
</GuideLayout>
